# Topic ACL for the feeder fleet. Anything not listed here is denied.
# Mosquitto's username is the client certificate CN (use_identity_as_username).
#
# Device ids match ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{2,31}$ and equal the certificate CN.
# `%u` below is replaced by that username.
#
# `pattern` rules apply to EVERY user, including `backend`. For `backend`
# they only expand to feeder/backend/..., which is no real device. That is
# why the id `backend` is reserved: a device cert with CN `backend` would get
# the backend rules below (command any device, read all devices).
# server/certs/make-certs.sh refuses to issue it. See server/README.md.

# --- Devices: own topics only --------------------------------------------
pattern read feeder/%u/cmd
pattern write feeder/%u/ack
pattern write feeder/%u/event
pattern write feeder/%u/state

# --- Backend service: client cert CN = backend ----------------------------
user backend
topic write feeder/+/cmd
topic read feeder/+/ack
topic read feeder/+/event
topic read feeder/+/state
